models.description:
Audit trail of all inventory changes.

Provides a complete, immutable history of every inventory adjustment, including reservations, allocations, returns, and corrections. This table supports forensic analysis and reconciliation.

Each transaction represents a single atomic change to inventory quantity and links to the source of that change (order, return, manual adjustment).

This table is critical for financial audit compliance and inventory reconciliation. It is append-only; records are never modified or deleted.

@link shopping_mall_order_items.id
@link shopping_mall_order_returns.id
@link shopping_mall_order_shipping.id

Notifications for inventory threshold breaches.

Tracks alerts generated when inventory levels fall below the configured min_stock_threshold. These alerts trigger notifications to sellers and may initiate automated reorder processes.

An alert is created when inventory_units.quantity drops below min_stock_threshold and is cleared when inventory increases beyond threshold.

This table provides historical visibility into stock issues and helps identify products with recurring low inventory problems.

@link shopping_mall_product_variants.id
@link shopping_mall_inventory_units.id

